#Day4
##Assignment-03
Test It, Check It, Own the Decision

#Easy
1. What makes a short-versus-detailed instruction test fair?
ANS: A test is fair when both instructions have the same task and goal. Only the level of detail should change so that the answers can be compared properly.
2. What is a consequential claim?
ANS: A consequential claim is a statement that can affect important decisions, safety, money, health, education, or people’s lives. It should be checked carefully before use.
3. Why should a student check a confident AI answer before using it publicly?
ANS: A student should check a confident AI answer because AI can sometimes provide incorrect or outdated information. Verifying the facts helps avoid mistakes and sharing false information.

#Intermediate
4. A short instruction gives a correct but general fest reminder. A detailed instruction includes the correct time, venue, and volunteer reporting time. Which answer better serves the fest committee? Explain why.
ANS: The detailed instruction better serves the fest committee because it provides complete and specific information. It mentions the correct time, venue, and volunteer reporting time. This helps students and volunteers
 understand what to do and when to arrive. It reduces confusion and makes the event easier to organize.
5. An AI writes a college exam date in a class-group message, but gives no source. What should the student do before forwarding it?
ANS: The student should verify the exam date using the official college notice, academic calendar, or college website. If necessary, the student should confirm it with a teacher or the examination department.
 The message should be forwarded only after confirming that the information is correct.

#Hard
6. Write one short instruction and one detailed instruction for the same real student task. State what must stay the same so the comparison is fair.
ANS: Short instruction: Write a reminder for students to submit their assignments.
Detailed instruction: Write a polite reminder for first-year BBA students to submit their assignments by Friday at 4:00 PM to their subject teacher. Keep the message under 60 words and use simple English.
What must stay the same?
The main task, purpose, and intended audience must remain the same. Only the amount of detail should change to make the comparison fair.
7. Change only one part of your detailed instruction, such as the audience or limit. Write what you expect to change in the new answer and what you will check after it runs.
ANS: I will change only the audience in the detailed instruction from first-year BBA students to final-year BBA students.
Expected change: The new answer will address final-year BBA students instead of first-year students. The wording may change slightly to suit the audience.
What I will check: I will check whether the answer follows the instruction, keeps the deadline and submission details correct, uses simple English, and stays within the 60-word limit. I will also ensure 
that the main purpose of the reminder remains the same.
